Industry Best Practices

Students are expected to:

Write clean, readable, and well-commented code.
Use meaningful variable names.
Follow PEP 8 coding standards.
Organize code into reusable functions.
Handle file-reading errors using exception handling.
Add chart titles, axis labels, legends (where applicable), and grids.
Ensure charts are professional, readable, and properly formatted.
Learning Outcomes

After completing this assignment, students will be able to:

Create professional scatter plots using Matplotlib.
Compare categorical data using bar charts.
Analyze numerical distributions using histograms.
Visualize proportions using pie charts.
Apply visualization best practices for real-world business datasets.
Develop publication-ready charts suitable for reports and presentations.
